WEBVTT

1
00:23:17.840 --> 00:23:20.640
My name is Lilian Okoro.

2
00:23:20.640 --> 00:23:23.640
Same University of Calabar, Nigeria.

3
00:23:24.200 --> 00:23:27.760
And my topic is closely related to

4
00:23:27.800 --> 00:23:31.200
what just happened
when this session began.

5
00:23:32.000 --> 00:23:35.000
You see a lot of struggles connecting,

6
00:23:35.960 --> 00:23:39.320
a lot of challenges with infrastructure.

7
00:23:39.320 --> 00:23:42.320
And so my topic is

8
00:23:43.240 --> 00:23:46.240
”Unsupervised

9
00:23:47.440 --> 00:23:50.440
Pedagogy

10
00:23:53.080 --> 00:23:54.640
and Electronic Literature

11
00:23:54.640 --> 00:23:57.880
under Infrastructural
Constraint: Experiences from Calabar.”

12
00:23:58.840 --> 00:24:03.120
Yeah, you already know
my name and [sound glitching] come in

13
00:24:03.120 --> 00:24:06.120
different shades and

14
00:24:07.280 --> 00:24:10.280
colors.

15
00:24:11.560 --> 00:24:14.560
And in Nigeria,

16
00:24:14.800 --> 00:24:18.560
when you hear, “Up NEPA!,” it's a common

17
00:24:18.560 --> 00:24:22.600
challenge that we have come to embrace.

18
00:24:22.760 --> 00:24:26.560
And when you talk about
electronic literature,

19
00:24:26.960 --> 00:24:29.760
power and Internet

20
00:24:29.760 --> 00:24:33.600
are key elements that must make

21
00:24:33.600 --> 00:24:36.600
electronic literature possible.

22
00:24:41.240 --> 00:24:43.680
And so I came up with

23
00:24:43.680 --> 00:24:46.640
the concept of unsupervised pedagogy
[sound

24
00:24:46.640 --> 00:24:49.640
glitching]

25
00:24:55.520 --> 00:24:59.520
teaching my students
electronic literature.

26
00:24:59.520 --> 00:25:02.960
The stage here now is power.

27
00:25:03.960 --> 00:25:05.920
The screen goes off;

28
00:25:05.920 --> 00:25:09.120
what happens to the learners?

29
00:25:10.000 --> 00:25:12.440
What becomes of that

30
00:25:12.440 --> 00:25:15.440
particular session of learning?

31
00:25:15.800 --> 00:25:20.000
I have come to realize
that the learning shouldn't

32
00:25:20.000 --> 00:25:23.720
stop when there's a power outage,
when there's Internet

33
00:25:25.240 --> 00:25:27.040
disconnection,

34
00:25:27.040 --> 00:25:30.760
the learners have to be equipped,
keep creating.

35
00:25:31.320 --> 00:25:34.320
Even during these

36
00:25:39.720 --> 00:25:40.520
infrastructural constraints.

37
00:25:40.520 --> 00:25:45.760
And that every performance begins
with a moment of uncertainty

38
00:25:45.800 --> 00:25:48.960
like we started now
and we are— and all that.

39
00:25:48.960 --> 00:25:54.280
Sometimes the light itself fails and
sometimes the stage changes unexpectedly.

40
00:25:54.400 --> 00:25:57.560
Yet the show must go on.

41
00:25:57.680 --> 00:25:59.720
That is the slogan in the theatre.

42
00:25:59.720 --> 00:26:04.000
So when these things happen,
what equips the students

43
00:26:04.480 --> 00:26:09.320
to continue to create
is what I call the Calabar

44
00:26:09.520 --> 00:26:13.360
model of unsupervised pedagogy.

45
00:26:14.200 --> 00:26:17.680
C is create authentic projects
for the learners,

46
00:26:18.280 --> 00:26:22.040
create projects
they can relate with, Then A,

47
00:26:23.880 --> 00:26:26.040
assign collaborative

48
00:26:26.040 --> 00:26:29.240
production roles.

49
00:26:30.440 --> 00:26:32.960
Let students be paired

50
00:26:32.960 --> 00:26:36.920
to reason together and assigned to create.

51
00:26:36.960 --> 00:26:40.120
Then lead them through building on

52
00:26:40.120 --> 00:26:43.240
different levels of reasoning.

53
00:26:43.240 --> 00:26:48.880
I say lead through scaffolding,
then adapt through improvization.

54
00:26:49.120 --> 00:26:53.800
You must learn to improvise
when what you need is not available.

55
00:26:54.200 --> 00:26:56.960
Then you create from your mind

56
00:26:56.960 --> 00:27:00.480
what should be present
until what you need is available.

57
00:27:00.520 --> 00:27:03.280
It may be your Internet, it may be power.

58
00:27:03.280 --> 00:27:06.680
Then build peer learning communities.

59
00:27:06.880 --> 00:27:10.840
Let the students work in groups
where they can criticize

60
00:27:10.880 --> 00:27:14.200
the ideas that come up,
either from the lecturer

61
00:27:14.280 --> 00:27:17.280
or from themselves.

62
00:27:17.560 --> 00:27:22.600
Then assign them to reflect.

63
00:27:22.640 --> 00:27:27.000
Finally, R, reinforce learner autonomy.

64
00:27:27.400 --> 00:27:31.520
When we do this during infrastructural

65
00:27:31.520 --> 00:27:35.040
constraint, the learning is not paused.

66
00:27:35.360 --> 00:27:37.440
Learning continues.

67
00:27:37.440 --> 00:27:41.800
The students continue to exchange ideas

68
00:27:41.800 --> 00:27:46.360
and eventually
the level of production is not reduced.

69
00:27:46.360 --> 00:27:51.160
Because once power is restored,
once Internet is restored,

70
00:27:51.240 --> 00:27:55.760
what has been generated in their mind,
their imagination,

71
00:27:55.800 --> 00:27:58.880
shouldn't be paused
when electricity stops.

72
00:27:59.640 --> 00:28:04.080
So electronic literature production begins
with teaching

73
00:28:04.080 --> 00:28:08.400
and learning—
that is, pedagogy—before technology.

74
00:28:08.440 --> 00:28:12.040
From this, so many things have emerged

75
00:28:12.040 --> 00:28:17.040
and we see that the
students even reason more

76
00:28:18.040 --> 00:28:19.880
flexibly when

77
00:28:19.880 --> 00:28:24.440
they are a bit constrained

78
00:28:24.520 --> 00:28:27.520
You see the [sound glitching]

79
00:28:38.120 --> 00:28:38.640
before

80
00:28:38.640 --> 00:28:43.920
even generating ideas from—
So the pause should— power

81
00:28:44.040 --> 00:28:48.480
outbreak, what— this song will always come
up, “keep pushing.”

82
00:28:48.520 --> 00:28:53.160
The show must go on
so students must keep learning.

83
00:28:53.320 --> 00:28:58.320
They must keep creating even when
there are infrastructural constraints.

84
00:28:58.720 --> 00:29:04.080
Once the teacher is able
to give the right information,

85
00:29:04.200 --> 00:29:07.760
the right
creative nuggets to the learners,

86
00:29:07.840 --> 00:29:11.360
it exposes them
to also exercise their mind,

87
00:29:11.600 --> 00:29:16.880
not confining them to what the teacher
has, you know, positioned.

88
00:29:16.880 --> 00:29:21.720
It gives them the leverage
to also use their mind while

89
00:29:23.040 --> 00:29:25.080
they are paused.

90
00:29:25.080 --> 00:29:29.280
And when they come back, they usually come

91
00:29:30.320 --> 00:29:33.240
back stronger.

92
00:29:33.240 --> 00:29:36.360
And some of the very outstanding

93
00:29:37.000 --> 00:29:40.160
literature that my students have recorded

94
00:29:40.160 --> 00:29:44.880
or have produced
come from when there is a pause,

95
00:29:44.880 --> 00:29:49.040
when there is a breakdown
in either Internet or power.

96
00:29:49.080 --> 00:29:54.520
So we shouldn't see the challenge of 
infrastructural constraint as something

97
00:29:54.520 --> 00:29:59.280
that should limit the Global South
from producing electronic literature.

98
00:30:01.640 --> 00:30:04.440
We should see it as an opportunity

99
00:30:04.440 --> 00:30:10.280
to explore the unsupervised pedagogy,
by preparing the students

100
00:30:10.280 --> 00:30:15.600
to become creators, rather
than passive recipients of knowledge.

101
00:30:16.200 --> 00:30:18.960
Every electronic literature comes

102
00:30:18.960 --> 00:30:22.520
from a creative mind
that has been prepared,

103
00:30:22.520 --> 00:30:28.080
and this preparation can come
even when the class is dark.

104
00:30:28.400 --> 00:30:31.400
When electricity and Internet

105
00:30:31.560 --> 00:30:35.960
become unavailable,
the creative process should not stop.

106
00:30:36.120 --> 00:30:39.120
We must encourage ourselves to reorganize

107
00:30:39.800 --> 00:30:43.920
into small groups,
continue writing, continue

108
00:30:43.920 --> 00:30:49.480
producing these electronic literatures
until such a time

109
00:30:49.480 --> 00:30:52.480
when these infrastructural

110
00:30:52.640 --> 00:30:55.640
constraints are under control.

111
00:30:56.120 --> 00:30:59.120
When infrastructure pauses,

112
00:30:59.600 --> 00:31:02.360
production should not pause.

113
00:31:02.360 --> 00:31:07.600
Unsupervised pedagogy prevents
creativity from pausing.

114
00:31:07.920 --> 00:31:10.920
The show must go on,

115
00:31:12.320 --> 00:31:15.320
always.

116
00:31:15.560 --> 00:31:17.360
Thank you.
